# Nougat OCR extraction stub

**Paper:** arXiv:2004.10344 — Smart & Mazziotti, *Efficient Two-Electron
Ansatz for Benchmarking Quantum Chemistry on a Quantum Computer*, Phys Rev A
103, 012420 (2021).

**Status (2026-07-05):** stub. Nougat rerun deferred per the backfill
free-endpoint / no-rerun contract. The paper text used for claims-table
construction in this replication was extracted via:

```
pdftotext -layout work/paper.pdf work/paper.txt
```

and human-verified against the PDF (see `report/REPORT.md` §1–§2). This
`extraction/nougat.mmd` file is a placeholder to satisfy the QC-100 backfill
artifact-inventory requirement; the substantive OCR-equivalent extraction
lives at `work/paper.txt`.

## To upgrade this stub to a real Nougat extraction

```
# On uicgpu (free A100 endpoint, per Rick's small-batch-OCR-to-uicgpu rule):
nougat work/paper.pdf --out extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base
mv extraction/paper.mmd extraction/nougat.mmd
```

Expected: `.mmd` (Mathpix-Markdown) with LaTeX-form equations, tables, and
figure captions preserved. Preferred over `pdftotext` for a paper this
equation-heavy — but not required for the current replication scope, which
turned on identifying six discrete claims and their testability status,
both of which the pdftotext extraction supports adequately.

